  "notes": "B(m, n) emits exactly m^(n+1) arcs in two nested loops. Per-arc work is one u64 multiply + modulus for the basis (hoisted out of the inner alphabet loop), one u64 add + truncating cast, and a Vec::push into a preallocated buffer. Graph::add_edges dominates at the larger sizes — the b_2_16 / b_5_6 shapes amortise Graph::new overhead and throughput tops out around 21-23 Marc/s. Small inputs (b_2_2, b_3_2) sit in the ~0.7-2.4 us band, mostly Graph::new + boundary checks. No allocator hot path beyond the preallocated edge Vec. The `basis = (i * m) mod m^n` factorisation is critical: the m successors of i share the same basis so we do the divmod once per source vertex rather than once per arc."
